00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:02.160
How did all of this happen?

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:03.565
Why is AI so good suddenly?

00:05:03.565 --> 00:05:06.660
The answer is the transformer model

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.100
which caused a paradigm shift

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:11.730
on how we build large
language models, LLM.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:14.190
By the way, this diagram
means nothing to me.

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:17.280
It makes me look smart, so
that's why I put it on there.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:18.210
Before transformers,

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:21.360
the best natural language
processing system used RNN,

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.670
and then it used LSTM,

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.620
but then Google Brain published a paper

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.860
in 2017 called "Attention is All You Need"

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:31.683
which is also my life's motto
because I'm a narcissist.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:34.980
The paper proposes a
simple neural network model

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.810
they call transformer, which is based

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:39.030
on the self attention mechanism

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:41.520
which I don't fully
understand, so I'll pretend

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.170
like I don't have time to explain it

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:47.130
but I also know that it allows
for more parallelization

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:49.350
which means you can throw more hardware,

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:51.780
more GPUs to make your training go faster

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.300
and that's when things got crazy.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:57.720
They kept adding more data
and also added more parameters

00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:59.430
and the model just got better.

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:00.480
So what did we do?

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:03.180
We made bigger models with more parameters

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:05.013
and shoved it a shit ton of data.

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:16.370
Sorry, I'm trying my best
here to make the model bigger.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:17.400
All right, fuck it.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:18.750
Anyway, that gave us ready

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:22.290
to use pre-trained transformer
models like Google's Bert,

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:26.700
and OpenAI's GPT, generative
pre-trained transformers.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:28.830
They crawled the whole
web to get text data

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:30.630
from Wikipedia and Reddit.

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:34.080
This graph shows you how many
parameters each model has.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:37.380
So as you can see, we've
been increasing the number

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:40.050
of parameters exponentially.

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:42.630
So OpenAI kept improving their GPT model

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:45.000
like how Goku kept
becoming stronger each time

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.890
he reached a new Super Saiyan form.

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:47.820
While editing this,

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:51.120
I realized how unhelpful the
"Dragon Ball" analogy was.

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.410
So I want to try again.

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:55.500
To recap, transformer was
the model architecture,

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:56.730
a type of neural network.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:07:00.690
Other types of models
would be like RNN and LSTM.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:03.270
Compared to RNN, transformers don't need

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.400
to process words one by one,

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:08.700
so it's way more efficient at
training with lots of data.

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:12.420
OpenAI used the transformer
model and pre-trained it

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:14.700
by feeding it a bunch of
data from the internet

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:18.630
and they called that
pre-trained model GPT-1.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:21.840
Back then, NLP models would
be trained from scratch

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:26.130
for a specific task like
translation or summarization.

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:29.280
Both transformer, we get to
pre-train the model first

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:31.560
then fine tune it for a specific task.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:34.830
Then for GPT-2, they did
the same thing, but more

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:39.360
and with a bigger model, hence
with 1.5 billion parameters,

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:41.160
and then with GPT-3,

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:45.210
they went crazy and gave
it 175 billion parameters.

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:47.190
However, just like raising a kid,

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:48.390
just shoving it with a bunch

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:51.750
of information unsupervised
might not be the best way

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:52.620
to raise a kid.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:53.940
She might know a lot of things,

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.430
but she hasn't learned proper
values from her parents.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:59.550
So that's why we have to fine
tune it, tell it what's right,

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:03.570
and what's wrong, how not to
be racist and clean up its act.

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:08.340
That's GPT-3.5, a more
fine-tuned version of GPT-3

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:11.070
with guardrails that can
be released to the public.

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:13.440
Now you have a decently well-behaved kid,

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:16.830
but you now want to show her
off, so you dress it up nicely,

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:20.040
get her ready for her first
job, AKA more fine tuning

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.840
with some supervised training

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:24.600
so it behaves properly as a chat bot.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.910
That way it's well packaged
and is ready to ship

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:28.980
to the world with a web UI.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:32.820
Okay, back to the original
shitty "Dragon Ball" explanation.

