"ChatGPT Tech is not
particularly innovative."

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:30.960
That is just massive copium.

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:32.400
Finally, we got Netflix,

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:34.380
who's too busy cracking
down on password sharing

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:35.463
to care about AI.

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:38.340
All right, what about us engineers?

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:40.170
What's the future for us?

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:41.190
The reality is

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:44.610
that GPT isn't replacing
anybody's job completely.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:46.890
Like most technological innovations,

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:48.720
that change can seem drastic

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:51.033
because the media loves dramatic titles.

00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:54.840
But if you're open-minded,
you have time to learn

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:57.300
about it and embrace it
rather than fighting it.

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:59.550
If you're a software engineer
and you feel threatened

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:03.660
by ChatGPT being able
to solve FizzBuzz, oof,

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:07.380
then you should maybe
consider becoming a YouTuber.

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:08.640
Just kidding.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:10.110
Please don't compete with me.

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:12.117
Though, you should incorporate ChatGPT

00:13:12.117 --> 00:13:14.040
and GitHub Copilot to your workflow.

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:16.890
It really removes tedious
parts of software engineering.

00:13:16.890 --> 00:13:19.830
If you're working in a new
language or API library,

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:22.380
you don't have to Google, sorry, Google,

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:23.970
you don't have to Google endlessly

00:13:23.970 --> 00:13:25.140
for the stuff you already know.

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:27.090
Just break down and describe your problem

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:29.880
to ChatGPT to get a huge headstart

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:33.060
or get good at coding alongside Copilot.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:34.920
If you structure your code base well

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:37.620
and write good comments that
describe what you want to do,

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:40.590
Copilot often gets the
logic problems right.

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.510
It's a symbiotic relationship.

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:44.640
Become the cyborg.

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:47.340
See, the trick here is that,
as a software engineer,

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:48.870
your job is to translate

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:52.290
and break down a business
problem into software problems.

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:54.750
Your job is to know what questions to ask

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:56.700
and what answers to accept.

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:58.230
In fact, here's my prediction.

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:00.690
GitHub Copilot is not
done innovating here.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:03.480
Their next big product
release will turn an issue

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:07.560
or PR description into an
actual full-blown code commit.

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:11.460
So as a software engineer in
2024, you better get real good

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:14.730
at writing GitHub issues
and reviewing PRs.

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:17.670
All right, that's it
for this ChatGPT video,

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:21.840
but I think this ChatGPT
narrative is just one battle

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:23.790
of a bigger AI war that's happening

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:25.830
between Microsoft and Google.

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:27.870
I'll talk about that next time.

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:29.790
See you and thanks for watching,

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:32.198
and remember to call your parents.

00:14:32.198 --> 00:14:35.531
(upbeat musical effect)

